cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AUTOPHAGE: Bare-Metal Polymorphic x86-64 Galois-Field Genetic Engine with Six-Kernel Lean 4.35.0 Verification"
message: "If you use AUTOPHAGE, its Lean 4.35.0 proofs, or its companion white paper, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
version: "1.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/0thernes/autophage"
url: "https://github.com/0thernes/autophage"
abstract: >-
  AUTOPHAGE v1.4.0 is a zero-dependency C11 bare-metal artificial-life and
  open-ended evolutionary engine in which 256-byte dual-strand organisms compile
  themselves via evolvable 8x8 F_2 ribosome matrices (VGF2P8AFFINEQB) into live
  native x86-64 RWX machine code with Galois-field polynomial recombination
  (PCLMULQDQ), 2x2 Cauchy MDS self-repair over GF(2^8), symplectic reversible
  Toffoli/Fredkin gates, POPCNT bit-erasure accounting, and 2-adic TZCNT
  kin-sensing. 48 Lean 4.35.0 theorems (zero Mathlib, zero sorry, zero
  native_decide) about Lean models of its finite-field, bitvector and ledger
  definitions, not its emitted machine code, are kernel-checked by Lean (lake
  build, leanchecker); the 48 comparator targets were also accepted by 6
  independent kernels in Ubuntu CI. Six of the 48 are one-line arithmetic or
  XOR identities, and the finite-field facts checked (for example the 30
  irreducible binary octics) are textbook results. Engine behaviour is tested
  by an 18-gate falsification suite (including 6 planted negative mutants).
  The work resolves no open problem.
